{"reference":"1 Chronicles 29","book":"1 Chronicles","chapter":29,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"David’s Preparation","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter can be read as presenting David’s preparations as broader than the materials named in his speech. Alongside the public offerings and Solomon’s installation, the account portrays the temple work as being prepared through organized leadership and shared support for Solomon’s task.","verse_refs":["1 Chronicles 29:1-22"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_chronicles_029_c122ca67278eb64f449cbefd"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}